storcli64 only, in its own directory.

The script probes for storcli/perccli with `command -v` and uses one if it is
staged. A stub in stubs-decomm would therefore always be found, and the common
case -- no vendor binary present, which is what the Ubuntu archive gives you --
could never be tested. Prepend this directory only for the cases that want a
RAID CLI to exist.
